{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism","id":1024701,"title":"Sadism, Psychopathy and parochial altruism","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-31T03:56:53-08:00","id":1024701,"title":"Sadism, Psychopathy and parochial altruism","content":"God day every one! It's again me with ideas of questionable quality.<br /> At the down of new year i will star steampank chronicle on homebrew lore but with CofD mechanics. And players already present to me their mostly evilish characters. This led me to question, can characters resist breaking point not because of their will (hight enough Composure+Resolve), not because of circumstance (selfdefense or achieving virtue), but because of their physiology? Here I propose to discuss in an amateur manner mental disorders and their effects on the mechanics. And i am not read yet Beast The Primordial.<br /> IMO, Integrity perfectly represent phycology of normal people (in game terms). But sadists and psychopaths not exactly mentally healthy people. But they can behave. And they can safer. Their disorder lay within empathy and social interaction.<br /> Most inborn psychopaths can have high Integrity (unlike normal people with low Integrity with obtained psychopathy). They can reflect their action. And understand where they action place mistreat. They can analyze emotions, but cant understand them. There they don't give a fuck for harming people or be harmed by others.<br /> With sadists matter more complicated. They can understand emotions but they retrieve joy for harming others. Even when they understand that's amoral. And they will continue to do this as long as it does not put them at risk. There we say &quot;just use original rules!&quot;. But sadist does not safer degenerative condition from Integrity loss. They don't become more insane, they become more corrupt (from their addiction to harm).<br /> And third in row but not last in meaning group - We Are. In our common nature embedded behavior of group rivalry. In social psychology this phenomenon is called <a href=\"http://www.nature.com/nature/journal/v442/n7105/abs/nature04981.html\" target=\"_blank\">parochial altruism</a>. In short terms we more love who include in &quot;our&quot; group and hate the most who disclude &quot;our&quot; group. We fill less empathy for those with whom we associate less ourselves. And safer the most when see how our most loved has been harmed.<br /> <br /> And there three merits i can propose.<br /> <br /> <b>SADIST</b> (** or ***)<br /> Prerequisites: Only on character creation, Resolve *** (sadist should have nerves for reaching his desire), Vice related to harming people<br /> Effect: on two dot version character does not safer from degenerative condition from Integrity loss. On three dot version selfdefens action grant autosuccess on breaking point.<br /> Drawback: character obtain Addicted Condition (Vice) with all the attendant.<br /> <br /> <b>Psychopath</b> (*****).<br /> Prerequisites: Only on character creation, Composure *** (psychopath should not give a fuck for anything)<br /> Effect: character never safer breaking point from social interaction (harming, killing, abuse - whatever what include interaction with humans)<br /> Drawback: every fail on empathy considered as dramatic fail.<br /> <br /> Third merit goes well with hate group system (from Hurt Locker). It's perfectly show how behave people with such ideology... But does not grant anything for saving your integrity.<br /> <br /> <b>Philosophy</b> (Style * to <i>let us</i><i> come up with more!</i>)<br /> Prerequisites: Status * or more in any hate group, Composure * or ** (a person should not be able to resist the influence of the crowd to him), Wits * or ** (should not be aware of his misbehavior).<br /> * <b>Our / Alien</b>: for each dot in merit character get bonus on Integrity roll when harming an alien person and penalize Integrity rall when harm our person<br /> *** <b>Holy War!</b>: when engaging in combat where obviously known enemy affiliation character can spend willpower to gain automatic success on each breaking point within battle. Character safer only one condition for all breaking point occurred within battle.<br /> Drawback: Storyteller should write down (or memorize it another way) each misdid maded by character in which it was possible to escape responsibility because of this merit, and remind each one of this with maximum (for max dot in merit) penalty on Integrity loss when character lost prerequisites.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T04:54:40-08:00","id":1024713,"title":"","content":"Merits are supposed to be boons foremost, with their drawbacks being consequences of overextending yourself. Are these boons to your character? Or anybody? Really?<br /> <br /> Putting aside how questionable statting up stuff like this is, I'd say sadism can already be represented by tweaking existing mechanics. Take Vice and Virtue, for example. Normally, I'd say take Sadistic as a Vice and be done with it. If you go further, you can have Sadistic as a Virtue. Now, mortals are supposed to have redeeming and positive qualities as Virtues by the rules, but a little adjustment to the base template will be okay it seems you are already approaching this whole thing in the &quot;Those people must have something fundamentally wrong with them&quot; perspective (one that I strongly disagree with, but just rolling with it for the moment). Go further and have them be immune to the universal breaking points of inflicting harm on others. This quality need not be inherent, and can be acquired.<br /> <br /> For the Merit, I have no idea why sadists would have high Resolve. The Resolve Attribute represents your patience and perseverance, and the ability to think straight in stress. Maybe the sadist develops that as he continues to inflict harm on others in a steady way, but I don't believe sadists are inherently strong-willed that others. By chance, did you put that in for the &quot;cool&quot; and &quot;badass&quot; factor that gets applied to criminals so often in pop culture?<br /> <br /> The same line of logic above applies to the Psychopath Merit above and its Composure requirement. Composure represents your ability to keep calm in stress and emotionally adjust to changes in the environment. Even heartless killers get upset when their plans go wrong and get caught, and feel fear when faced with their own pain. And besides, &quot;psychopathy&quot; isn't even a singular phenomenon, unlike sadism which can be roughened up with sandpaper to be fit in anti-social behavior.<br /> <br /> Lastly, parochial altruism I see more apt as a series of dice modifiers on breaking point rolls that interact with group psychology rather than a Merit.<br /> <br /> And once again, in case I haven't made it clear, I really don't think these are suit to be represented mechanically. CofD got rid of Derangements from its 1E version for a damn good reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T09:34:52-08:00","id":1024789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1024713#post1024713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Those people must have something fundamentally wrong with them&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! this is not the flaws of parenting, It is innate qualities that make us who we are. For the majority of the population is a group confrontation. And for chosen ones it's specific mental disorder.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1024713#post1024713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Merit, I have no idea why sadists would have high Resolve</div> </div> </div> </div>May be then Presense? Make him look pushy, annoying. To show his ability to grab the victim by the balls. May be this is skill. My point there to show that the sadist does not change, nothing (except other breaking points) can shatter inner world, she already sick as is. The whole system is placed in the two rules, everything else is tinsel: sadist does not get to acquire condition on breaking point associated with torture people (any other BP do it); sadist has a addiction on her activities. The behavior of the character in such a way not formed by acquired condition. But character herself become less and less human. May be on zero Integrity she become Beast if not loosing character (for lose to the addiction)? <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1024713#post1024713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Resolve Attribute represents your patience and perseverance</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1024713#post1024713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Composure represents your ability to keep calm in stress and emotionally adjust to changes in the environment</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1024713#post1024713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;psychopathy&quot; isn't even a singular phenomenon</div> </div> </div> </div>translation difficulties.<br /> For first two I mean that the ability to do what you do not want to do, and for the second don't do what you wont to do. For psychopathy - general lack of empathy and emotions as is.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1024713#post1024713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same line of logic above applies to the Psychopath Merit above and its Composure requirement</div> </div> </div> </div>For demonstration of emotional dystrophy of psychopath. You cant provoke what does not presence here. You cant inspire who does not interested. But instead due social unexperience if he lose for it he lose complitly. Maybe we should hang the dramatic failure on all failed social interactions?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1024713#post1024713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, parochial altruism I see more apt as a series of dice modifiers on breaking point rolls that interact with group psychology rather than a Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could not agree. But! Force of reaction to such interaction much depends on how strong association of character with the group. Status and size of the group does not represent this force. Or we just give +/-2 for Status merit and for Bonded Condition.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1024713#post1024713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And once again, in case I haven't made it clear, I really don't think these are suit to be represented mechanically. CofD got rid of Derangements from its 1E version for a damn good reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>As i say i will run quite evil party. If i just turn off BP (some general or their oven) integrity cease to work. but if i do nothing, the game will end quickly in the nuthouse.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1024713#post1024713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This quality need not be inherent, and can be acquired.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically It cant. Parochial altruism can delay PTSD, but do not get rid of it. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1024713#post1024713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go further and have them be immune to the universal breaking points of inflicting harm on others.</div> </div> </div> </div>That about psychopathy!<br /> Happy New Year, comrade!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T15:42:28-08:00","id":1024926,"title":"","content":"I'm not a Psychopath, I can be very empathetic to other people, but I'm a sexual sadist who gets off on the pain and humiliation of people in very specific situations. <br /> <br /> But as I mentioned I have lots of empathy and compassion as well. <br /> <br /> In fact I think having a strong capcity for empathy is one of the most important traits for a Dom/Sadist, not just for ethical reasons either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T00:23:03-08:00","id":1025019,"title":"","content":"There are some major flaws in your understanding of sadism, which is understandable. It's not something I've seen popular media address well ever, but being a sadist doesn't mean somebody lacks empathy, or that harming other people never causes them emotional distress. It's a kink, and like any other it's situational and context dependent and varies from person to person. I'm a sadist, and in most circumstances seeing other people in pain is not something that I enjoy, quite the opposite; it bothers me a lot. It took me a long time to accept that it was a thing I wanted in any circumstance at all. The first time I started having sadistic thoughts about a friend it left me hating myself so much that I wanted to kill myself. I didn't understand how I could want to harm somebody who was so kind to me and to other people in general. The answer is I didn't, and I don't. I want to make someone suffer <u>in the moment</u>, in way that leaves them with good memories instead of trauma. Before I understood S&amp;M it didn't occur to me that was possible or made any sense but it absolutely is and does. There's no more of a contradiction in that than there is in saying I enjoying moderately strenuous hikes in good weather but would be miserable doing a 13 mile barefoot slog in the pouring rain. <br /> <br /> If you want mechanics to represent somebody who really isn't bothered by the suffering of others breaking points already give you pretty significant leeway to determine what bothers your character enough to roll, and where to assign modifiers. The chart in the core calls itself out as a suggestion, you can always adjust the numbers to suit your game. Beyond that, Hunter has a system for replacing normal breaking points with more character specific compulsions. It would need a little updating but the general idea should work fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T03:55:42-08:00","id":1025045,"title":"","content":"Oh, I am sorry, people! no harm intended! If this may calm you, &quot;Nana to Kaoru&quot; manga is one of my favorite. I really don't mean normal people. And you are normal.<br /> What i mean is humans who deviate above deviation. I talk about people who generally sick. Can you refer yourself being sick? I think no. It's about men with triple X chromosome and other <u>physiological</u> deviation. Normal people cant become physiological psychopath. But they can adapt for this (Integrity by Attrition from Hurt Locker represent it's perfectly). I don't think you will like refer yourself to Chikatilo or other maniacs...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1025019#post1025019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want mechanics to represent somebody who really isn't bothered by the suffering of others breaking points already give you pretty significant leeway to determine what bothers your character enough to roll, and where to assign modifiers. The chart in the core calls itself out as a suggestion, you can always adjust the numbers to suit your game. Beyond that, Hunter has a system for replacing normal breaking points with more character specific compulsions. It would need a little updating but the general idea should work fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont read yet. May be you can refer? And I also wont to hear about integrity system in Beast The Primordial.<br /> My main point here, True maniac can't be broken by normal BP (maybe only supernatural and natural not social). Most mental condition impose some behave (and one character through story can have many suchlike) when maniac have only one but aggravated. But does it mean that he can not be broken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T05:33:46-08:00","id":1025056,"title":"","content":"Many have brought up sadism, but I am going to address psychopathy for a moment. Psychopathy is, first and foremost, a genetic quirk. Some people are born with less empathy for others and a desire for power. These people aren't killers, child molesters, or any of that. Perhaps they will become lawyers or police, or any number of other positions. They contribute to society.<br /> <br /> Now, psycho killers that we are familiar with from media are another matter. They are the result of a combination of the above genetic quirk combined with (ususally childhood) trauma/abuse. In game terms, they already have low Integrity, broken people with psychological issues they have trouble dealing with. Often, killing is the result of trying to gain some control over themselves and the world around them, a way to release built up stress and frustration and gain catharsis.<br /> <br /> Anyways, the point is that psychopathy, barring trauma, is little different from a normal person. Psycho killers have mental trama and broken minds, reflected by virtually no Integrity, and should have no special considerations in merit form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T07:43:25-08:00","id":1025071,"title":"","content":"&quot;Deviation&quot; is a lot more complicated than simply &quot;normal&quot; or &quot;sick&quot;. There are several ways in which I'm <i>not</i> normal (by which I mean I fall into groups representing 2% or less of the population), but they're mostly not things that are immediately obvious. Some of them impair my daily functioning, like a learning disability that often leads me to forget important items when I leave the house to go somewhere, among other organizational difficulties. Some of them don't directly cause me problems but mean I can't intuitively understand the way the majority of people think, like being on the ace spectrum. Some of them are just weird quirks that don't seem to do anything, like growing up cis-male but discovering at 17 that I also have one partially formed ovary and thus technically fall within the intersex umbrella. Speaking of which, intersex people aren't any less capable of empathy or remorse than the general population.<br /> <br /> To answer your questions about Beast and mechanics in general though: Human characters with a propensity for murder have always been represented with low integrity/morality. Slashers in first edition had Morality 4 or less, and Beast's primary antagonists typically mirror this with low integrity scores. Not because all Heroes have low integrity, but because low integrity Heroes are vastly more likely to go out killing. First edition Morality did have the idea that characters can reach a point where certain Sins no longer bother them, and you could always go that route and ignore the recommendation that murder always be a breaking point.<br /> <br /> Beasts themselves handle things very differently. They lack an integrity score, and what they have in its place is Satiety, which is not subject to the same rules. Beasts can be as violent, cruel, and depraved as they wish, and doing so tends to increase their Satiety. Beast flips the sanity/morality bar concept; it rewards Beasts for being cruel by filling their hunger bar, and leaves the punishment aspect to the enemies that kind of behavior inevitably creates and attracts, and to what the players and characters are willing to live with in pursuit of a fix. All told, Beast is an excellent game to explore sadism and amorality, either as characters struggling to find healthy outlets for violent tendencies, or just as an outlet for the players themselves. I get that, sometimes you want to play terrible fictional people, because you can do all that stuff and not worry about consequences since the victims only exist in the group's imaginations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T14:23:24-08:00","id":1025164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1025056#post1025056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many have brought up sadism, but I am going to address psychopathy for a moment. Psychopathy is, first and foremost, a genetic quirk. Some people are born with less empathy for others and a desire for power. These people aren't killers, child molesters, or any of that. Perhaps they will become lawyers or police, or any number of other positions. They contribute to society.<br /> <br /> Now, psycho killers that we are familiar with from media are another matter. They are the result of a combination of the above genetic quirk combined with (ususally childhood) trauma/abuse. In game terms, they already have low Integrity, broken people with psychological issues they have trouble dealing with. Often, killing is the result of trying to gain some control over themselves and the world around them, a way to release built up stress and frustration and gain catharsis.<br /> <br /> Anyways, the point is that psychopathy, barring trauma, is little different from a normal person. Psycho killers have mental trama and broken minds, reflected by virtually no Integrity, and should have no special considerations in merit form.</div> </div> </div> </div>When was they broke? Do they have just bigger Integrity pool? Or have boost (from merit) on Integrity rall? Can adult lawful-nutral psychopath become chaotic-evil?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1025071#post1025071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts themselves handle things very differently. They lack an integrity score, and what they have in its place is Satiety, which is not subject to the same rules. Beasts can be as violent, cruel, and depraved as they wish, and doing so tends to increase their Satiety. Beast flips the sanity/morality bar concept; it rewards Beasts for being cruel by filling their hunger bar, and leaves the punishment aspect to the enemies that kind of behavior inevitably creates and attracts, and to what the players and characters are willing to live with in pursuit of a fix. All told, Beast is an excellent game to explore sadism and amorality, either as characters struggling to find healthy outlets for violent tendencies, or just as an outlet for the players themselves. I get that, sometimes you want to play terrible fictional people, because you can do all that stuff and not worry about consequences since the victims only exist in the group's imaginations.</div> </div> </div> </div>EXCELLENT! Not an integrity, but Social Awareness. Where trait represent power of reaction. And five question, which should determine why people wold think it's not normal crime but something what should be hunted. Or just all crimes against the person or humanity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T17:59:28-08:00","id":1025214,"title":"","content":"As someone's bestfriend is the closest a person can be to a psychopath (the actual definition of psychopath is still highly debated), this is very inaccurate. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1025164#post1025164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When was they broke?</div> </div> </div> </div>They broke when circumstances would cause them to have too many breaking points I guess?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do they have just bigger Integrity pool? Or have boost (from merit) on Integrity rall? </div> </div> </div>No. Psychopathy doesn't have anything really to do with Integrity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can adult lawful-nutral psychopath become chaotic-evil? </div> </div> </div>Alignment doesn't exist. People don't work that way... and chaotic-evil doesn't equal murderer or crazy or anything so it's a redundant question anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T20:47:17-08:00","id":1025270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(the actual definition of psychopath is still highly debated)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugum. It's spectral. Some say it's just quarrelsomeness (what in some national medical system not false). But here we look for something what define, merge a line.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They broke when circumstances would cause them to have too many breaking points I guess?</div> </div> </div> </div>They rall Integrity loss when two BP appear per scene or three BP per session? Or we just don't give mental condition on integrity loss until psychopath reach 4 dot integrity?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alignment doesn't exist. People don't work that way... and chaotic-evil doesn't equal murderer or crazy or anything so it's a redundant question anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Integrity. Point here can psychopath when mature and adult evolve from Victorian to villain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-02-2017, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T07:41:53-08:00","id":1025429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1025164#post1025164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When was they broke? Do they have just bigger Integrity pool? Or have boost (from merit) on Integrity rall? Can adult lawful-nutral psychopath become chaotic-evil?</div> </div> </div> </div> Can we not reduce people that are utterly mentally broken and driven by psychological needs into such degrading terms?<br /> <br /> In fact, I'm going to say this. Your entire exercise is flawed because its based on the idea of an &quot;evil game.&quot; Sadism is not evil. Psycopathy is not evil. Merits are never going to reflect what you want them to because of this.<br /> <br /> Vampire and Mage both have ways of negating breaking points and turning them into banes / paradox. The Code, ala Hunter 1e, did similar. I would use a similar mechanic - gain a Persistant Condition in exchange for negating something as a breaking point. Its quick, its easy, and best of all? Its personalized to each character and not stereotyping psychological issues that aren't entirely understood.<br /> <br /> Honestly, though, if you want to do an evil game about people with a culture of murder and decaying empathy for others, I recommend just playing Vampire. That's kind of what Humanity does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:02:23-08:00","id":1025435,"title":"","content":"In the end, I also think its important to note that, for the most part, Integrity is not Morality. Integrity measures your mental health in responce to discovering things about the supernatural, how you heal from supernatural trauma, and what moral foundations you're willing to violate in order to survive or cope with encountering the supernatural. In general, if its something that a character wouldn't be bothered by in the first place, I don't think its appropriate for Integrity in the first place.<br /> <br /> Integrity is kind of like a Santity meter from a Call of Cthulhu game. You struggle and fight against the occult, which warps your very understanding of the world. If you're not doing something related to that kind of thing, then it really isn't a big deal. You shouldn't need merits to reflect that kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T17:38:16-08:00","id":1026779,"title":"","content":"I'll try to keep it simple, since we are clearly having issues with translation.<br /> <br /> 1- You understood nothing of psychology. Nothing. Don't try.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you can't understand. But explaining things will take far more than this thread.<br /> <br /> 2- Integrity isn't being good. Is being sane. Most people break if they harm others. Some don't.<br /> <br /> 3- You don't need new rules. You need new uses to old rules. Try this:<br /> <br /> Psychopaths change all BP for harming other people to similar BP for harming herself. A psychopath don't care for others, but care a lot for itself.<br /> <br /> Sadistic people have a Vice or similar Condition if needed toward hurting people (most do not). Pay attention to how they answer BP questions at Character Creation.<br /> <br /> Parochial Altruism makes people have distinct BP for in-group and out-group.<br /> <br /> 4- If your players like being monsters, let them be. If you don't like it, talk to them. The game won't break because of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T00:44:53-08:00","id":1026903,"title":"","content":"Oh! How pretty: there are easily offended people! How many delicious FAT!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your entire exercise is flawed because its based on the idea of an &quot;evil game.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's is an evil game. Players will do many evil things. But if they will do only evil things game will shattered. I need some mediation there, where they can be evil but in frame. I needed a system that describes it, and I got it.<br /> BP mechanics in normal circumstances enough for me without integrity pool: accumulation of stress (represented by mental condition received on BP) illustrate itself enough. There i can just give only one condition for each clinical mental divination and its will be enough. But the whole point in Integrity pool that player can lost character for madness. Like death on health like as madness on integrity. The problem is that those psychopaths and sadists, about which we speak, initially abnormal (not their fault in it). Not mad or insane but abnormal.<br /> Satiety (from beast) mechanics better for my need.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You understood nothing of psychology. Nothing. Don't try.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you can't understand. But explaining things will take far more than this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we get personal, then i have conflictology degree. Its have plenty of psychology. In particular describing where, when and under what circumstances a person can harm another person and dont fill remorse after that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Integrity isn't being good. Is being sane. Most people break if they harm others. Some don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which break and which not?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You don't need new rules. You need new uses to old rules. Try this:</div> </div> </div> </div>For what kind of reason Satiety system was created?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If your players like being monsters, let them be. If you don't like it, talk to them. The game won't break because of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>As i say above i dont need that my monsters always behave like monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T03:13:19-08:00","id":1026946,"title":"","content":"The Satiety system was created for supernatural creatures whose Soul is replaced with a Hunger. Not humans.<br /> And your conflictology degree seems a bit suspect because the others are completely correct about how psychology works.<br /> If you want somehing unrealistic, just ask for that advice, but Integrity as it works right now is completely realistic in regard to people who are sadists or psychopaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T04:47:01-08:00","id":1026966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026946#post1026946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Satiety system was created for supernatural creatures whose Soul is replaced with a Hunger. Not humans.<br /> And your conflictology degree seems a bit suspect because the others are completely correct about how psychology works.<br /> If you want somehing unrealistic, just ask for that advice, but Integrity as it works right now is completely realistic in regard to people who are sadists or psychopaths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, really? There is no people with questionable sense of empathy? There no people with physiological deviation in nervous system? There is no people with general abnormality in their mind?<br /> I say, Integrity system mostly represent PTSD and its diversity. But there are people who does not prone to PTSD. And there people whom psyche crack under stress and they discover not so bright side of them. And if most people do not fall under the latter last two cases, there are few who are. And if normal people can change under stress (for better or worse) this few doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T04:54:06-08:00","id":1026968,"title":"","content":"My biggest problem here, is that you're saying &quot;we're playing an evil game of evil&quot; here's a couple of merits which represent such people 'Sadist&quot; and &quot;psychopath.&quot; and at that point, I'm like what the hell. I know several sadists, due to my involvement in bdsm. And I can assure you, several of them are the most kind and awesome people I've yet to meet. Being a sadist, does not mean that you're going to do something against other people's desires. It doesn't mean you won't either.<br /> <br /> So in short, justl ike any other person, a sadist (or a person with any other fetish/kink) can be both good and evil. Good people who find that they are sadists, find consenting playpartners, who are into receiving pain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Bad people, who find that they are sadists, might start assaulting people.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T05:38:02-08:00","id":1026979,"title":"","content":"You want help with running an evil game? That's fine. Its trivially easy to not apply Integrity towards evil actions if you're a bad person. Integrity is designed to measure the shock and trauma you recieve, and how much dealing with the supernatural will change you. If you're playing characters with zero qualms about tormenting others, then simply don't roll Integrity. The section on Integrity again and again stresses that you should take individual personalities into account. Or use any other suggestions in this thread.<br /> <br /> The problem is that you are displaying a marked misunderstanding of not only how Integrity works, but sadism, psychopathy or in-group mentalities. Reduced empathy for others, true or not, has <i>nothing</i> to do with Integrity. Nothing. Integrity is not Morality. I repeat. Integrity does not measure morality. It measures how well you deal with supernatural trauma and revelations as well as how far you are willing to change in order to survive/cope with interacting with the supernatural. The anti-social behaviors you want to function have no relationship to how Integrity works. The two are completely separate issues. And that's not even touching on the fact that having psychopathic, sadistic, or sociopathic tendacies does not equate to anti-social behavior, like you are saying it does.<br /> <br /> <br /> Integrity measures how much of a toll your sense of self and mental stability has suffered.<br /> Humanity cares about empathy and relating to humans. But there's nothing wrong with playing low Humanity vampires - they can function in vampire society, and live hiding in human society well enough with just a single dot your choice of the right disciplines.<br /> Harmony doesn't care about empathy towards others. In fact, it FOSTERS the in-group, out-of-group mentality you want through seeing everyone not-pack as prey.<br /> Wisdom cares about control over magic, not empathy or treating others nicely. Its been discussed how cold, calculated killers actually would have high Wisdom, since they're so precise.<br /> A Promethean's pilgrimage cares about understanding humans and becoming mentally balanced, which can include a lack of empathy and a desire to inflict pain. Humanity isn't always nice.<br /> Clarity cares about avoiding the trauma you suffered before, and reinforcing the sense of self.<br /> Cover only cares about acting like the role you adopt. If you are playing the part of an anti-social killer, then your Cover goes up.<br /> Satiety doesn't care about what actions you take. Its your supernatural fuel.<br /> <br /> <br /> Only one of the 2e Integrity-equivalents cares about the evil behaviors you want in your game. The others simply don't measure it at all. All the games, in fact, allow &quot;evil&quot; in one manner or another as playable entites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-05-2017, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T06:18:51-08:00","id":1026990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It measures how well you deal with supernatural trauma and revelations as well as how far you are willing to change in order to survive/cope with interacting with the supernatural</div> </div> </div> </div>And what should i do with lioris share of examples? Where third about how you harm others, third how others harm you and third how third party harm others?<br /> And during game supernatural BP are less frequent than BP on violence.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Integrity measures how much of a toll your sense of self and mental stability has suffered.</div> </div> </div> </div>The human psyche includes a mechanism prohibiting harm to another person from your own group. The &quot;OUR&quot; group has become much wider in modern society than just a &quot;family&quot; or &quot;tribe&quot;. but a person can include herself in group on other grounds (by the district of residence, on a national basis, by belonging to a subculture). This behavior is typical of young people, to cause the so-called feeling of community (perhaps not entirely correct translation). However, in general such markers as belonging to the group in general does not emerge, and any normal person watching someone's trouble will sympathize with the suffering. The absence of this properties of residents of big cities is a big social problem.<br /> That is, I'm trying to say, your mental stability will shatter when you harm other. You subconscious will cry from guilt and crave for forgiveness. In typical situation. And not so pathetic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only one of the 2e Integrity-equivalents cares about the evil behaviors you want in your game. The others simply don't measure it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arigato gosai masu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T13:04:17-08:00","id":1027236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026903#post1026903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! How pretty: there are easily offended people! How many delicious FAT!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't do this, it only invites antagonistic responses from other forum users and is a Terms of Use violation..</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T14:52:30-08:00","id":1027309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026903#post1026903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's is an evil game. Players will do many evil things. But if they will do only evil things game will shattered. I need some mediation there, where they can be evil but in frame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just asking: why the game will shatter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026903#post1026903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I needed a system that describes it, and I got it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it works for you, that's good, anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026903#post1026903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BP mechanics in normal circumstances enough for me without integrity pool: accumulation of stress (represented by mental condition received on BP) illustrate itself enough. There i can just give only one condition for each clinical mental divination and its will be enough. But the whole point in Integrity pool that player can lost character for madness. Like death on health like as madness on integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Degrading Integrity isn't the same as insanity, though most insane people will have low integrity. Integrity measures how strained is your ability to cope with stress. In the end, it is just a way to find a bonus or penalty over the roll for BP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026903#post1026903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that those psychopaths and sadists, about which we speak, initially abnormal (not their fault in it). Not mad or insane but abnormal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't only an extremely simplistic way to describe such things, indeed wrong for sadists. It isn't relevant. The game mechanics don't need to change for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026903#post1026903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we get personal, then i have conflictology degree. Its have plenty of psychology. In particular describing where, when and under what circumstances a person can harm another person and dont fill remorse after that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't my intent to get personal, nor do I think our respective degrees should play any role in this. But if you want, I'm a psychologist, specialized in mental disorders, and my main focus is on psychopathy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026903#post1026903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which break and which not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone breaks, just under distinct stimulus. That's why BP can be customized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026903#post1026903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As i say above i dont need that my monsters always behave like monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Not that I face it a lot, but why is it a problem specifically in your chronicle?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026966#post1026966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, really? There is no people with questionable sense of empathy? There no people with physiological deviation in nervous system? There is no people with general abnormality in their mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there are. They just don't work as you think, nor need more extraneous rules to work in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026903#post1026903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say, Integrity system mostly represent PTSD and its diversity.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be precise, BP system represents PTSD as a whole, Integrity represents an aspect of this, coupled with specific BP, Composure + Resolve roll, its results, and the Conditions assigned. Integrity alone is a pretty minor part of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026903#post1026903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there are people who does not prone to PTSD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely wrong. There are people that are prone to PTSD under distinct circumstances. Those people can be prone to PTSD under circumstances most people can even think desirable, while circumstances that would completely break most people can mean nothing to those.<br /> <br /> Some break under very strange circumstances, but virtually everyone is prone to PTSD. (There are actual people who aren't as much, but they aren't the ones you think)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026903#post1026903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there people whom psyche crack under stress and they discover not so bright side of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can be either represented as a Condition brought by the BP, as a change in BPs, or simply as role play, like every other aspect of a character's personality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026903#post1026903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if normal people can change under stress (for better or worse) this few doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, but they can. Just because they won't easily change in the way of ceasing to be as you describe them, doesn't mean they don't change, evolve and adapt in their own way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026990#post1026990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And during game supernatural BP are less frequent than BP on violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>During <u>your game</u>, I presume.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1026903#post1026903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The human psyche includes a mechanism prohibiting harm to another person from your own group.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is far more complex than that, and includes more than one psychological mechanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T00:16:19-08:00","id":1027478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just asking: why the game will shatter?</div> </div> </div> </div>As i say i have three munchkin (not as much as munchkin as trolls) as a players. Be fellow powergamer it's normal circumstances in that group. Be righteous fellows they obey written law. Only. And addition wot i declare on start of campaign. It's just hard to cope with them on fly. I mast show logic behind my reasons (pure dominance does not work what's logical). With inly normal character they do many questionable thing. But i learn one thing about them: they hate to lose pieces (as integrity dots) of their character. And they learn that i learn. And in this campaign they declare character with high and absolute tolerance to violence. And one of them can rall EX.success constantly despite dicepool. Normal integrity just will not work on THEM.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Degrading Integrity isn't the same as insanity, though most insane people will have low integrity. Integrity measures how strained is your ability to cope with stress. In the end, it is just a way to find a bonus or penalty over the roll for BP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point there is player lost character on zero Integrity.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't my intent to get personal</div> </div> </div> </div>Then don't assume that i understand nothing in psychology.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm a psychologist, specialized in mental disorders, and my main focus is on psychopathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Internet no bode know or bother that you are cat.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Not that I face it a lot, but why is it a problem specifically in your chronicle?</div> </div> </div> </div>They tend crawl into whitespace of world. Improvisation not hard trick to me but be only phlegmatic i have slower nervous system than them and just dont catch on them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely wrong. There are people that are prone to PTSD under distinct circumstances. Those people can be prone to PTSD under circumstances most people can even think desirable, while circumstances that would completely break most people can mean nothing to those.<br /> <br /> Some break under very strange circumstances, but virtually everyone is prone to PTSD. (There are actual people who aren't as much, but they aren't the ones you think)</div> </div> </div> </div>And there you cross out one of two general BP.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That can be either represented as a Condition brought by the BP, as a change in BPs, or simply as role play, like every other aspect of a character's personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>After that they don't receive new condition in such situation. They use that Condition.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">During <u>your game</u>, I presume.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let Throwing them vampires!<br /> In one of translation (maybe it's translator gag) of cWoD VtM i read about the approximate ratio of humans and supernatural (vampires particular). It's about 1 vampire to 100000 humans. In other books (or CofD particular) i don't met such information. If we assume that ratio for other supernatural spices then we can suggest that's we have 1 SN creature to 10000 human. How often should normal person (not sleepwalker or ghoul or bloodkin) meet supernatural phenomena? If he does not do it on purpose.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is far more complex than that, and includes more than one psychological mechanism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I declared amateur manner in that topic in firs post! Nothing complex! Only arbitrary suggestion! But if you insist we can continue.<br /> There many kind of situation where man can harm each other. In lioris part people usually do not realize the consequences of their actions. Not they wont specifically harm or kill other, they just have grudge of frustrated that can aggravate by alcohol. Understanding comes after dids. In most common places.<br /> But also we have not so common but more brutal event where people harm each other on daily base. War never change. That where ideology (and parochial altruism as psychological mechanism) kick. On East front of European theater of war died about 13+ (lets not discus exact number - it's too speculative) millions military on both sides. In Red army on moment of war end have served about 10 millions of citizens. And if some of them broke most don't. Why? Because they don't kill <u>humans</u> - they kill &quot;fascist <u>vermin</u>&quot;. &quot;\u0424\u0430\u0448\u0438\u0441\u0442\u043a\u0443\u044e \u0413\u0430\u0434\u0438\u043d\u0443&quot; - old man pronounced this words with such gusto and hate. It becomes apparent that the image of &quot;the enemy&quot; (not hatred for Germans people but &quot;the enemy&quot;) in it is still alive. And, obviously, this way there is enough reason to gain a foothold in his mind.<br /> Of course, you can yell at each corner, parochial altruism thats and thats. It's simple. For adult it's does not enough to become nuts (government need to nurture this fillings not just pasture image of themselves but also pasture image of &quot;the enemy&quot;). But where it's enough? Can you recall school ostracism for all newcomers? Or odd man out?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-06-2017, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:43:28-08:00","id":1027645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1027478#post1027478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As i say i have three munchkin (not as much as munchkin as trolls) as a players. Be fellow powergamer it's normal circumstances in that group. Be righteous fellows they obey written law. Only. And addition wot i declare on start of campaign. It's just hard to cope with them on fly. I mast show logic behind my reasons (pure dominance does not work what's logical). With inly normal character they do many questionable thing. But i learn one thing about them: they hate to lose pieces (as integrity dots) of their character. And they learn that i learn. And in this campaign they declare character with high and absolute tolerance to violence. And one of them can rall EX.success constantly despite dicepool. Normal integrity just will not work on THEM.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds like they're rules-lawyering you? That's going to be very difficult with Integrity, because Integrity, by its very nature, is not designed to have hard rules. Its meant to be entirely subjective.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, why not stick with 1) revelation of supernaturals, 2) supernatural trauma, and 3) chosen breaking points from Character Creation? That way, its easier on everyone, and drives home the mysterious aspects of the CofD, not knowing what's out there, instead of worrying about anything else?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Point there is player lost character on zero Integrity. </div> </div> </div> Do they? I see no rule to that effect in the book. Humanity 0 vampires are lost to the Beast, Wisdom 0 mages lose control over their magic, but Cover 0 demons can regain new covers, and Satiety 0 Beasts can feed back up. Things just kind of stop measuring at Integrity 1, with no explanation of what happens if you go lower. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-06-2017, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:26:01-08:00","id":1027679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1027478#post1027478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As i say i have three munchkin (not as much as munchkin as trolls) as a players. Be fellow powergamer it's normal circumstances in that group. Be righteous fellows they obey written law. Only. And addition wot i declare on start of campaign. It's just hard to cope with them on fly. I mast show logic behind my reasons (pure dominance does not work what's logical). With inly normal character they do many questionable thing. But i learn one thing about them: they hate to lose pieces (as integrity dots) of their character. And they learn that i learn. And in this campaign they declare character with high and absolute tolerance to violence. And one of them can rall EX.success constantly despite dicepool. Normal integrity just will not work on THEM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, your problem isn't Integrity, but how you work with Breaking Points. Let them have extremely high tolerance to violence. They will have less XP because BP grant XP. Also make the world respond. If they are troublesome, people will react to them. The world of CofD have police, government, authorities. The supernaturals also have authorities of their own. If you still feel the need to use game rules to control them, make other BPs. A psychopath could roll for BP at any damage taken, even bashing, because they are sometimes too sensible to being harmed. Tell your players that if the characters are so immune to violence to others, they will have to take strange and common things as Breaking Points. Someone with arachnophobia will roll for BP at seeing a spider too close. BPs can be much more, the book only shows some examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1027478#post1027478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point there is player lost character on zero Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong. Read the book again. Integrity doesn't low to 0. It stops at 1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1027478#post1027478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then don't assume that i understand nothing in psychology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't assumed nothing, nor wanted to offend. What I meant was that your reasoning seemed too off. You missed the target with what you said then. I didn't assumed, I interpreted from what you said. What you said was wrong in too many places.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1027478#post1027478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Internet no bode know or bother that you are cat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, you did it first. But at least now I think I know with what I'm dealing here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1027478#post1027478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They tend crawl into whitespace of world. Improvisation not hard trick to me but be only phlegmatic i have slower nervous system than them and just dont catch on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the problem? What is the problem if your players want to do mindless violence? What is the problem if your players want to be as strong as possible? What in this is harming the fun of the group? Those are serious questions. I need precise answers to understand your group dynamics and the true nature of the problem at hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1027478#post1027478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there you cross out one of two general BP.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem at all. Even general BPs are just examples. Create new ones if you need. Or keep with 2, or 1, or none at all. Your players don't seem interested on this aspect of the game, so why bother?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1027478#post1027478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After that they don't receive new condition in such situation. They use that Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they receive new Condition, because you can consider that the Persistent Condition doesn't count anymore for this limit. They keep it, and reap XP from it, and new rolls bring new Conditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1027478#post1027478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let Throwing them vampires!<br /> In one of translation (maybe it's translator gag) of cWoD VtM i read about the approximate ratio of humans and supernatural (vampires particular). It's about 1 vampire to 100000 humans. In other books (or CofD particular) i don't met such information. If we assume that ratio for other supernatural spices then we can suggest that's we have 1 SN creature to 10000 human. How often should normal person (not sleepwalker or ghoul or bloodkin) meet supernatural phenomena? If he does not do it on purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game is about dealing with the supernatural. It doesn't matter how rare it is in the world in general (and the numbers aren't quite that, anyway), the PCs are special, the protagonists of your story, and they deal with the supernatural as frequently as you want. If you don't want much, no problem at all. But, as I said: <u>your table</u>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1027478#post1027478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I declared amateur manner in that topic in firs post! Nothing complex! Only arbitrary suggestion! But if you insist we can continue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I insist on nothing. I said it isn't even important to this discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1027478#post1027478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There many kind of situation where man can harm each other. In lioris part people usually do not realize the consequences of their actions. Not they wont specifically harm or kill other, they just have grudge of frustrated that can aggravate by alcohol. Understanding comes after dids. In most common places.<br /> But also we have not so common but more brutal event where people harm each other on daily base. War never change. That where ideology (and parochial altruism as psychological mechanism) kick. On East front of European theater of war died about 13+ (lets not discus exact number - it's too speculative) millions military on both sides. In Red army on moment of war end have served about 10 millions of citizens. And if some of them broke most don't. Why? Because they don't kill <u>humans</u> - they kill &quot;fascist <u>vermin</u>&quot;. &quot;\u0424\u0430\u0448\u0438\u0441\u0442\u043a\u0443\u044e \u0413\u0430\u0434\u0438\u043d\u0443&quot; - old man pronounced this words with such gusto and hate. It becomes apparent that the image of &quot;the enemy&quot; (not hatred for Germans people but &quot;the enemy&quot;) in it is still alive. And, obviously, this way there is enough reason to gain a foothold in his mind.<br /> Of course, you can yell at each corner, parochial altruism thats and thats. It's simple. For adult it's does not enough to become nuts (government need to nurture this fillings not just pasture image of themselves but also pasture image of &quot;the enemy&quot;). But where it's enough? Can you recall school ostracism for all newcomers? Or odd man out?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, we are talking about distinct degrees, here. A single BP roll, even failed, isn't an actual instance of the disease called Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder. It is just a symptom of great stress. In that sense, if few war veterans broke completely, almost all of them come from war extremely traumatized, including by the things they did to enemies.<br /> <br /> It doesn't mean the phenomenon you are describing doesn't exist. It exists, along with a few others. But it work to a degree, not completely.<br /> <br /> Either way, it is still irrelevant. We are not discussing psychology, we are discussing your proposed rules. No one here is saying that those things don't exist. We disagree with two completely different things:<br /> <br /> One, we disagree with your assumptions about <u><b>how</b></u> those things work. Specially on the subject of sadism.<br /> <br /> Two, we disagree with your rules. I'm trying to show you how you can use the system as is to better represent what you want.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, I'm probably the last one even bothering to continue this, but that won't last. It is a little hard to understand you given the apparent translation difficulties, but your aggression over being disagreed with isn't subtle. If anything I said offended, you can call me on that here or by PM, and I will apologize. If you keep trolling here and there in your immense posts, I'll quit talking to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T08:35:58-08:00","id":1027690,"title":"","content":"As a high-functioning psychopath, I can provide some personal insight on the issue. One of the best ways to approximate my own psychological makeup in CoD terms is to ignore and discard any and all Breaking Points that are related to harming others or being exposed to their suffering, especially if the subject can reasonably assume it was necessary or really, really convenient for one's welfare, to protect the persons and things one cares for (psychopaths can form love and friendship bonds, even if they are shallower and more conditional than for other people), or to advance one's vision of the greater good (psychopaths can have ideals).<br /> <br /> At most, if the subject has a well-developed, not-empathy-based sense of responsibility or a perfectionism streak, you can have a BP if harm to others would result from one's gross incompetence or sloppiness. Or it might be a result of violating one's ideals in other ways: e.g. if I care a lot about science or art, I may feel bad harming an important scientist or artist or letting such a person come to harm by my inaction, even if I do not usually give a damn about strangers.<br /> <br /> There is simply no conceivable circumstance I can realistically picture myself suffering a PTSD-like backlash from harming others or witnessing their suffering, up to and including killing someone in cold blood, if I am genuinely persuaded it was somehow necessary or inevitable. Let psychopath characters replace BP related to harming others or witnessing their suffering with others related to harming the self, betraying their self-image, and other issues based on the rest of their personality. E.g. for someone like me, a case could certainly be made for dramatic failures or violation of my own ideals being a BP.<br /> <br /> I won't make comments on the rest of the discussion, because translation issues are giving me serious comprehension trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-07-2017, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T09:12:31-08:00","id":1027706,"title":"","content":"Ok. I've been avoiding posting in this thread because I found the core concept distasteful, and didn't want to threadcrap, particularly when it's clear there is a language barrier that is probably skewing perceptions on both sides. But I have to respond to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1027478#post1027478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As i say i have three munchkin (not as much as munchkin as trolls) as a players. Be fellow powergamer it's normal circumstances in that group. Be righteous fellows they obey written law. Only. And addition wot i declare on start of campaign. It's just hard to cope with them on fly. I mast show logic behind my reasons (pure dominance does not work what's logical). With inly normal character they do many questionable thing. But i learn one thing about them: they hate to lose pieces (as integrity dots) of their character. And they learn that i learn. And in this campaign they declare character with high and absolute tolerance to violence. And one of them can rall EX.success constantly despite dicepool. Normal integrity just will not work on THEM.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's clear that your issue here stems from a contentious group dynamic. If your players' rules lawyering is causing problems for you as a storyteller, the solution is not to double down on tecnical readings and precise rulings. It's to <i>talk to your players</i> about it. If you're feeling trolled by your own players, nobody is going to be having a good time. Besides, Chronicles of Darkness is written with the assumption that the players (including the storyteller) will interpret the rules using their own best judgment, not adhere to the letter of the rules in spite of the spirit of the rules. That's why the books are written in natural language and why so many things are made to be flexible and tailored to the individual character. If you insist on interpreting the rules as if they were written in technical language, all it will lead to is frustration. Both for you and for your players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1027478#post1027478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point there is player lost character on zero Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually not true. And I'm surprised, if your players are such rules lawyers, that they haven't pointed this out to you yet. Nowhere in the book does it say you lose your character when their Integrity drops to zero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T02:29:03-08:00","id":1028079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your players' rules lawyering is causing problems for you as a storyteller</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says that i don't enjoy it? I barely dont wont to lose all of the time.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong. Read the book again. Integrity doesn't low to 0. It stops at 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then Integrity pool is most useless thing. If you wont a penalty for Integrity rall use all and only mental Condition what present on character as a counter for penalty - there is no less or more clear mind with no condition.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But at least now I think I know with what I'm dealing here.</div> </div> </div> </div>A male cat?<br /> <br /> But it is necessary to put an end to this. If the administration twice visited the topic, it says that you're doing something wrong. Moreover, the goal was achieved. I should apologize to <b>Charlaquin</b> and <b>Darksider </b>for disturbance and commotion. I should apologize to <b>monteparnas </b>and <b>MCN </b>for provoking them unconsciously (although I still do not agree with their view point). And I am very grateful to <b>Irioth </b>and <b>HelmsDerp </b>for their revelations.<br /> Some one! Close this <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">threadcrap</div> </div> </div> </div> for greater good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T06:33:19-08:00","id":1028129,"title":"","content":"The Moderators here don't use distinct accounts for personal use and to moderate, so you only have to worry with the red letters.<br /> <br /> And threads aren't closed this way. We'll all live with the possibility of someone resurrecting this from the dead threads in a couple years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T07:43:39-08:00","id":1028145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028079#post1028079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says that i don't enjoy it? I barely dont wont to lose all of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You called your players trolls for it. That implies what they're doing is bothering you - that's what trolling is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028079#post1028079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then Integrity pool is most useless thing. If you wont a penalty for Integrity rall use all and only mental Condition what present on character as a counter for penalty - there is no less or more clear mind with no condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't supposed to be a penalty. It's supposed to create drama and emulate tropes of the supernatural horror genre. Mechanics that punish players for undesired character actions are bad design, because they foster a contentious &quot;player vs. GM&quot; group dynamic, like the one you are currently struggling with. If you don't want your players to act a certain way, just tell them that instead of &quot;taking away part of their character in the form of Integrity dots.&quot; All that does is escalates the out-of-character conflict, without actually fixing the real problem.'That's why D&amp;D hasn't made Paladins lose their class abilities if their alignment shifts for the past nine years, and it's why Chronicles of Darkness changed from Morality and Derangements to Integrity and Conditions. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028079#post1028079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it is necessary to put an end to this. If the administration twice visited the topic, it says that you're doing something wrong. Moreover, the goal was achieved. I should apologize to <b>Charlaquin</b> and <b>Darksider </b>for disturbance and commotion. I should apologize to <b>monteparnas </b>and <b>MCN </b>for provoking them unconsciously (although I still do not agree with their view point). And I am very grateful to <b>Irioth </b>and <b>HelmsDerp </b>for their revelations.<br /> Some one! Close this for greater good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just posting as a fellow CofD fan. Apart from the post Darksider gave you the warning for, you haven't done anything against the rules. I had just been keeping out of the thread until now because I wasn't interested in participating in a discussion about simulating anti-social personality disorder and sadism as Merits that removed Breaking Points. If anything, they should probably be Conditions. I decided to comment because you expressed that your reasoning for doing so was to continue to escalate a conflict with your players that you created by trying to punish character behavior you didn't want them to engage in with Breaking Points. The discussion doesn't need to end if you don't want it to, I just wanted to share my opinion - that you would be better off talking to your players about what you and they want out of the game, instead of using their characters to fight a proxy battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-07-2017, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T12:09:34-08:00","id":1028223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028079#post1028079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some one! Close this<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1027706#post1027706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">threadcrap</div> </div> </div> </div> for greater good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, and when I said &quot;threadcrap&quot;, I didn't mean your thread is crap. I meant that I didn't want to come in and crap on it. Threadcrap is sort of a colloquial term we use on these forums to mean posting in a thread with no purpose other than to express displeasure with the topic. When I say &quot;I avoided this thread because I didn't want to threadcrap&quot;, I mean &quot;I didn't have anything nice to say, so I didn't say anything.&quot; Once I had something I felt was worth contributing to the discussion, I did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T12:11:25-08:00","id":1028224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You called your players trolls for it. That implies what they're doing is bothering you - that's what trolling is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cultural differences: country where i live people are not easily offended by trolling. Becoming a victim of trolling is a sign of ignorance.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> out-of-character conflict</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such a conflict. And here it is not that I do not accept some characters' behavior (and the players). How to be so elaborate? Even in their own language is difficult to formulate (and here comes the understanding on how much it clear to the public abroad, when half of the phrases I write myself, and the other half with the help of Google, and it is not clear what it is better). Aspiration mechanics has become my salvation: I immediately fell to the need to come up with reasons why the characters must do something (ie to go on a quest). In general, the Integrity also became for me relief. Whether it goes crazy characters or not - is to take care of players themselves. In the end, we played without any Wisdom, while MtA 2ed has not yet been published. Although after we still have not started to use Wisdom - only one of us shares the &quot;official position&quot;. Well, to hell with mages - they <b>are</b> <u>Mages</u>.<br /> However, here we are gathered to play maniacs. Not mages, vampires or werewolves. Mortal maniacs. And what? Yet since free God-Machine update, I remember a wonderful phrase &quot;People always have a breaking point on murder&quot; or something like that. And here I found a cut diamond. How is it? Science knows many cases where people are killing each other and thus remain sane. It could be assumed that within the gaming terms, they rall an exceptional success. However, a certain group of persons, or persons with certain circumstances can do it on a regular basis. As I wrote, I would have really performed it as a condition in a normal game. But! There is a lot of blood and burnt bodies! Hurt Locker allows you to create on a start a completely nightmarish pyromaster (pyrokinesis 5 + Psychokinetic combat 5 + Psychokinetic Resistance + legendary occultism + 10 willpower + Pyromania as Vice). In terms of normal rules there should be plenty of BP on violence. And what is the use of them, if for character it is not important that they don't behave like people? And I also know that sadists not without empathy, psychopaths can suffer, and PTSD is it latent until a certain time. Throw a pity and can not leave. So I wanted to get the rules that I can explain to my players and they will be able to work with them themselves. And if I do this wrong, here, in fact, begin either trolling or abuse.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The discussion doesn't need to end if you don't want it to</div> </div> </div> </div>There two signs that discussion should be halted at least for a time.<br /> Second, i have a filing that we are talking in different languages (figuratively). Maybe it is because we really are speakers of different languages (hence the different understanding of the world). Maybe because we belong to different worldviews. Nevertheless, the conversation began to resemble &quot;And yet they can!&quot; - &quot;No, they can not!&quot; at the same position did not move despite the arguments and their severity.<br /> And, well, firstly, as i said, i received that mechanic what i wonted. Maybe it is a bit like Satiety. Lets call it Mania (anyway i don't like Genius as a system).<br /> Mania replaces Integrity. Mania Pool is empty at the start. When a character performs any action which that would cause Breaking Point to any other character, maniac should rall not on Integrity loss but on self-restraint (flip modifiers from Integrity modifiers chart). If succeed on rall he does not add point to Mania and should take mental Condition as a sublimation of his desires. If failed he unconsciously commits actions inflame his mania, which will leave behind more evidence (and and how the interpretation of this add dot to his Mania Pool). Every second point adds dice to the pool for the actions aimed at finding and identifying the maniac. This bonus can be interpreted as a penalty on the actions aimed at concealing identity and traces. Every second point grant dot in Destiny merit (from MtA 2ed) for character.<br /> The focus of personal questions shifted from the negative feelings during the Breaking Point on positive feelings.<br /> Yes, it's not sadism or psychopathy, but it's work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-07-2017, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T14:07:54-08:00","id":1028262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028224#post1028224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cultural differences: country where i live people are not easily offended by trolling. Becoming a victim of trolling is a sign of ignorance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about being offended or not being offended. The purpose of trolling is to upset the victim. By saying your players are trolling you, you are expressing that they are doing something with the purpose of upsetting you. Whether or not they succeed in upsetting you isn't important, the point is that your players are apparently playing a game of &quot;let's mess with the GM&quot; instead of playing a game of Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028224#post1028224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no such a conflict. And here it is not that I do not accept some characters' behavior (and the players). How to be so elaborate? Even in their own language is difficult to formulate (and here comes the understanding on how much it clear to the public abroad, when half of the phrases I write myself, and the other half with the help of Google, and it is not clear what it is better).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is understandable. There is clearly a significant communication problem due to translation problems. Sorry I can't meet you half way, since I don't speak any other languages besides English.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028224#post1028224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aspiration mechanics has become my salvation: I immediately fell to the need to come up with reasons why the characters must do something (ie to go on a quest). In general, the Integrity also became for me relief. Whether it goes crazy characters or not - is to take care of players themselves. In the end, we played without any Wisdom, while MtA 2ed has not yet been published. Although after we still have not started to use Wisdom - only one of us shares the &amp;quot;official position&amp;quot;. Well, to hell with mages - they <b>are</b><u>Mages</u>.<br /> However, here we are gathered to play maniacs. Not mages, vampires or werewolves. Mortal maniacs. And what? Yet since free God-Machine update, I remember a wonderful phrase &amp;quot;People always have a breaking point on murder&amp;quot; or something like that. And here I found a cut diamond. How is it? Science knows many cases where people are killing each other and thus remain sane. It could be assumed that within the gaming terms, they rall an exceptional success. However, a certain group of persons, or persons with certain circumstances can do it on a regular basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I think this is a major point of miscommunication. I'm going to try to express this as simply as I can, please feel free to ask me to rephrase anything the translation doesn't make sense. The Integrity system doesn't represent characters going insane. It represents a character's response to traumatic events and actions, and for most people, killing others is traumatic. But, if that rule doesn't suit your chronicle, you can change it. Removing murder as a Breaking Point or swapping Integrity for a different system, that's fine. But saying that there's a problem with the Integrity system because some people don't go insane from committing murder doesn't make sense, because Integrity doesn't measure sanity. Besides that, murder doesn't make anyone go insane, it's just traumatic for most people. If your chronicle is about playing characters for whom murder is not traumatic, that's fine. But tying that to anti-social personality disorder (the proper diagnostic term for what has been referred to as psychopathy in this thread), or to sadism (not an actual mental condition, but a preference for certain behaviors in sexual situations) is problematic because it implies very negative, and very inaccurate things about people who have those conditions, especially when so connected with talk of &quot;insanity&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028224#post1028224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I wrote, I would have really performed it as a condition in a normal game. But! There is a lot of blood and burnt bodies! Hurt Locker allows you to create on a start a completely nightmarish pyromaster (pyrokinesis 5 + Psychokinetic combat 5 + Psychokinetic Resistance + legendary occultism + 10 willpower + Pyromania as Vice). In terms of normal rules there should be plenty of BP on violence. And what is the use of them, if for character it is not important that they don't behave like people?</div> </div> </div> </div>The use of Integrity in the normal rules is to create drama and emulate tropes of the supernatural horror genre. Often in supernatural horror media, characters who experience the supernatural, the traumatic, or both, often have extreme reactions, such as becoming shaken and unable to focus on a task that would normally be easy, becoming spooked and making stupid mistakes like &quot;splitting up to cover more ground&quot;, or feeling survivor's guilt for having lived through an encounter with a Thing That Should Not Be. In some extreme examples they might go catatonic or start to question reality. The Integrity system is primarily about modeling those reactions to trauma, in a more nuanced way than just having a pool of &quot;sanity points&quot;. It also models similar reactions to personal trauma, such as experiencing something related to the worst thing a character has ever done, or taking another human life. At no point is it meant to punish players for their character's actions. One of the big issues with 1st edition's Morality system is that it was often perceived as a system of punishing wrong character actions, and Integrity was specifically designed to correct that issue with Morality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028224#post1028224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I also know that sadists not without empathy, psychopaths can suffer, and PTSD is it latent until a certain time. Throw a pity and can not leave. So I wanted to get the rules that I can explain to my players and they will be able to work with them themselves. And if I do this wrong, here, in fact, begin either trolling or abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't completely understand what you are saying here, but I get the sense that you're looking for a system other than Integrity that will better suit the needs of your group. That's perfectly fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028224#post1028224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There two signs that discussion should be halted at least for a time.<br /> Second, i have a filing that we are talking in different languages (figuratively). Maybe it is because we really are speakers of different languages (hence the different understanding of the world). Maybe because we belong to different worldviews. Nevertheless, the conversation began to resemble &amp;quot;And yet they can!&amp;quot; - &amp;quot;No, they can not!&amp;quot; at the same position did not move despite the arguments and their severity.<br /> And, well, firstly, as i said, i received that mechanic what i wonted. Maybe it is a bit like Satiety. Lets call it Mania (anyway i don't like Genius as a system).<br /> Mania replaces Integrity. Mania Pool is empty at the start. When a character performs any action which that would cause Breaking Point to any other character, maniac should rall not on Integrity loss but on self-restraint. If succeed on rall he does not add point to Mania. If failed he unconsciously commits actions inflame his mania, which will leave behind more evidence (and and how the interpretation of this add dot to his Mania Pool). Every second point adds dice to the pool for the actions aimed at finding and identifying the maniac. This bonus can be interpreted as a penalty on the actions aimed at concealing identity and traces. Every second point grant dot in Destiny merit (from MtA 2ed) for character.<br /> The focus of personal questions shifted from the negative feelings during the Breaking Point on positive feelings.<br /> Yes, it's not sadism or psychopathy, but it's work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sounds like you've figured out a system that will suit your chronicle. I think people are objecting to your associating it with anti-social personality disorder and sadism, not to your use of a different system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T01:01:20-08:00","id":1028460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether or not they succeed in upsetting you isn't important, the point is that your players are apparently playing a game of &quot;let's mess with the GM&quot; instead of playing a game of Chronicles of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>If line of conduct not clear for them because of rules whose fault is it?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But saying that there's a problem with the Integrity system because some people don't go insane from committing murder doesn't make sense, because Integrity doesn't measure sanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>No! Integrity system work perfectly for representing PTSD in character. Only issues with it i have that Integrity pool. What do he represent? After i read Stryx Chronicle and MtA 2ed i misconcluded that mortals also drop out from game. Because otherwise I do not understand why he was here at all. In another game on the homebrew world, I generally abandoned Integrity Pool. Although left the system itself. Although, I confess, for the most part due to the fact that Integrity Pool held a place on the charsheet. However, the game does not lose.<br /> If Integrity Pool does not identify a gradual descent into the depths of madness then why is it needed at all? What identifies a gradual loss of Integrity? Because the problems themselves are represented in the Conditions. And the mind has a tendency to adapt to the problems. In other words, if a person is aware of their problems and if the problem is not overpowering him. it is likely that by getting rid of their problems, he will be more prepared for the same situations. Not vice versa (as represented by Integrity Pool modifiers). Or we can say that it's a system that is not required to meet the reality. Allegedly, this is the vision of the developers. And to stay at his. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides that, murder doesn't make anyone go insane, it's just traumatic for most people. </div> </div> </div>I also know that's if people go insane after stress it's because they have some latent form of serious mental illness (schizophrenia or paranoia - your choice). In most of the neuroses we even do not pay attention. I'm afraid there was no accuracy on my part. I did not mean (though certainly think so) that on loss of Integrity people are going crazy (condition is responsible for this). I meant that the players themselves can determine when and where a character experiences Breaking Point.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But tying that to anti-social personality disorder (the proper diagnostic term for what has been referred to as psychopathy in this thread), or to sadism (not an actual mental condition, but a preference for certain behaviors in sexual situations) is problematic because it implies very negative, and very inaccurate things about people who have those conditions, especially when so connected with talk of &quot;insanity&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, my bad. I concluded hastily. When players rolled out in front of me a handful of bastards, the first thing I asked myself, who is less prone to PTSD. Here, in fact, I came to realize that I can not use Integrity as is.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> supernatural horror genre </div> </div> </div>I asume that players will generate most of horror. And mostly supernatural: they choose infected carrier, pyromancer, mind ninja and psyche vampire.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the big issues with 1st edition's Morality system is that it was often perceived as a system of punishing wrong character actions, and Integrity was specifically designed to correct that issue with Morality. </div> </div> </div>As i said characters do not see their dids as harmful (for them). They do not suffer from it, they enjoy it. In fact, the Mania is the same Integrity, only inverted reverse. In terms of the mechanics the character experiences the same effects, but the concept twist on the wrong side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T09:15:17-08:00","id":1028577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028460#post1028460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If line of conduct not clear for them because of rules whose fault is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't the rules' job to dictate a code of conduct. It's the job of the group to determine that for themselves. If you have a code of conduct in mind and you didn't tell your players so, it's your fault they don't know it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028460#post1028460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No! Integrity system work perfectly for representing PTSD in character. Only issues with it i have that Integrity pool. What do he represent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Integrity represents the wellbeing of the character's soul.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028460#post1028460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After i read Stryx Chronicle and MtA 2ed i misconcluded that mortals also drop out from game. Because otherwise I do not understand why he was here at all. In another game on the homebrew world, I generally abandoned Integrity Pool. Although left the system itself. Although, I confess, for the most part due to the fact that Integrity Pool held a place on the charsheet. However, the game does not lose.<br /> If Integrity Pool does not identify a gradual descent into the depths of madness then why is it needed at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's needed to determine what bonuses or penalties to apply to Breaking Point rolls. As a character's Integrity drops, the penalties to Breaking Point rolls Increase, making it more likely for them to roll a Failure or Dramatic Failure and gain a Condition or a Persistent Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028460#post1028460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What identifies a gradual loss of Integrity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being exposed to the supernatural or traumatic damages the character's soul, and makes it more difficult for them to cope with future trauma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028460#post1028460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the problems themselves are represented in the Conditions. And the mind has a tendency to adapt to the problems. In other words, if a person is aware of their problems and if the problem is not overpowering him. it is likely that by getting rid of their problems, he will be more prepared for the same situations. Not vice versa (as represented by Integrity Pool modifiers). Or we can say that it's a system that is not required to meet the reality. Allegedly, this is the vision of the developers. And to stay at his.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't meant to accurately reflect the effects of post-traumatic stress disorder, if that's what you mean. We're not talking about developing symptoms of schizophrenia after having been shell shocked in a war. We're talking about &quot;I saw a ghost and it spooked me.&quot; It's meant to reflect the tropes of the supernatural horror genre, and in the supernatural horror drama, characters get worse and worse at coping with the horror they experience as the story progresses and they are exposed to more and more traumatic events.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028460#post1028460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also know that's if people go insane after stress it's because they have some latent form of serious mental illness (schizophrenia or paranoia - your choice). In most of the neuroses we even do not pay attention. I'm afraid there was no accuracy on my part. I did not mean (though certainly think so) that on loss of Integrity people are going crazy (condition is responsible for this). I meant that the players themselves can determine when and where a character experiences Breaking Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Players do have some say over when and where their character's experience Breaking Points. The Storyteller also has some say. That's what the Five Questions are for - to help the Storyteller determine what should or shouldn't trigger a Breaking Point for the character, and to give the player some say in that decision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028460#post1028460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, my bad. I concluded hastily. When players rolled out in front of me a handful of bastards, the first thing I asked myself, who is less prone to PTSD. Here, in fact, I came to realize that I can not use Integrity as is.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cool. Sounds like you know what you need for your game, and that's a good thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024701-sadism-psychopathy-and-parochial-altruism?p=1028460#post1028460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asume that players will generate most of horror. And mostly supernatural: they choose infected carrier, pyromancer, mind ninja and psyche vampire.<br /> <br /> As i said characters do not see their dids as harmful (for them). They do not suffer from it, they enjoy it. In fact, the Mania is the same Integrity, only inverted reverse. In terms of the mechanics the character experiences the same effects, but the concept twist on the wrong side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, you're playing a game with very different assumptions than standard mortal Chronicles of Darkness. So it makes sense that you would need a different system, as Integrity is specifically designed to model the mounting trauma of (mostly) ordinary people caught up in supernatural weirdness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}